.TH DIGINET-PROBE 1 2026-10-19 "libdiginet" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
diginet-probe \- first test of a Digidesign Control|24 or ProControl surface
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B diginet-probe
.B \-i
.I interface
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B diginet-probe
.B \-\-fd
.I n
.B \-\-mac
.I mac
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B diginet-probe
wakes the desk cabled to
.IR interface ,
moves fader 1 to mid-travel, lights and clears strip 1 MUTE, writes OMX1 to strip 1's
scribble strip at two addresses and asks what shows, then logs and decodes every command the
desk sends for 60 seconds. It sends the disconnect frame on exit and ends with one summary
line per open question of the protocol it can answer.
.PP
It opens a raw packet socket and needs the
.B cap_net_raw
capability:
.PP
.RS
sudo setcap cap_net_raw=ep /path/to/diginet-probe
.RE
.PP
The packages set it on install.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-i " interface" "\fR, \fP\-\-interface " interface
The network interface the desk is cabled to.
.TP
.BI \-\-fd " n"
Use the already open descriptor
.I n
instead of opening a socket; it must carry whole Ethernet frames.
.TP
.BI \-\-mac " mac"
This host's MAC address, with
.BR \-\-fd .
.TP
.BI \-\-desk " mac"
Talk to this desk only.
.TP
.BR \-\-checksum " " zero | sum
The header sum of the frames sent: the body sum (default) or zero.
.TP
.BI \-\-keepalive " s"
Keepalive interval in seconds (default 10).
.TP
.BI \-\-listen " s"
How long to log the desk (default 60).
.TP
.BI \-\-wait " s"
How long to wait for the desk's announce (default 30).
.TP
.BI \-\-answer " s"
How long to wait for each answer (default 60).
.TP
.B \-\-touch\-test
Command fader 1 to 25%, send no echo, and report what the fader does while its cap is held
and after release.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print the usage.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 every step was acknowledged; 2 usage error; 3 the desk is in another host's session and
nothing was sent; 4 no desk answered; 5 the desk did not acknowledge our data.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR setcap (8),
.BR getcap (8),
.BR tcpdump (8)
